(Title) Tj
T*
(A Two-Year Prospective Evaluation of Web-Delivered Therapeutic Intervention for Anxiety) Tj
T*
(Disorders in Preadolescents: Study Design and Methodological Framework) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Anxiety disorders remain highly prevalent in school-age populations, yet access to) Tj
T*
(specialized mental health services remains limited. This protocol describes a prospective) Tj
T*
(randomized trial comparing technology-assisted therapeutic intervention against digital) Tj
T*
(informational control in Finnish preadolescents screened for anxiety. We will enroll) Tj
T*
(approximately 465 children aged 10-13 years identified through population-based screening.) Tj
T*
(The intervention arm will receive structured web-based modules \(10 sessions\) combined with) Tj
T*
(periodic remote clinical support. The control arm will receive standard psychoeducational) Tj
T*
(digital materials. Participants will be assessed at baseline, 12 months, and 24 months) Tj
T*
(post-randomization using validated caregiver and youth self-report scales. Primary) Tj
T*
(analyses will employ linear mixed-effects regression to compare anxiety symptom) Tj
T*
(trajectories between arms. Secondary analyses will examine moderators including baseline) Tj
T*
(severity, gender, and treatment engagement. We will also assess functional impairment,) Tj
T*
(mood symptoms, and parental psychological adjustment. This design allows for evaluation of) Tj
T*
(both immediate and sustained effects of the intervention.) Tj
ET
